  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345324",
      "title": "Arrays & Array Methods like map()",
      "sourceHash": "b6cd4694368b4325bd8478baea8092fd7953657343ecdf8891eee73ab60a66cb",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 3.81,
          "en": "Now besides objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.81,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "another crucial JavaScript value type are arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 11.01,
          "en": "Though, technically, arrays are objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.01,
          "end": 14.04,
          "en": "but they are special kinds of objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.04,
          "end": 17.49,
          "en": "Now, an array is created by using square brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.49,
          "end": 20.01,
          "en": "opening and closing square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.01,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "And the idea behind an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 27.06,
          "en": "simply is that you can create a list of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.06,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "So where objects allow you to group values together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 32.82,
          "en": "with key-value pairs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.82,
          "end": 36.72,
          "en": "the idea behind arrays is to have just values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.72,
          "end": 39.03,
          "en": "which are stored in a certain order",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.03,
          "end": 43.47,
          "en": "and which can be accessed by their position in that list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "So for example here, if I have an array of hobbies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 50.26,
          "en": "let's say Sports, Cooking, and Reading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.01,
          "end": 55.16,
          "en": "if I have such an array, I can access the array values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.16,
          "end": 60.16,
          "en": "by using square brackets after the name of the variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.44,
          "end": 63.93,
          "en": "or constant that stores my array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.93,
          "end": 66.063,
          "en": "So by using these square brackets here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.05,
          "end": 70.85,
          "en": "And then there, I use the index, as it's called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.85,
          "end": 73.653,
          "en": "of the element I want to output in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.55,
          "end": 76.89,
          "en": "Now the index starts at zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.89,
          "end": 79.5,
          "en": "So Sports here has an index of 0,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.5,
          "end": 82.85,
          "en": "Cooking has an index of 1, Reading has an index of 2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.73,
          "end": 85.17,
          "en": "If I wanna output Sports here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.17,
          "end": 89.22,
          "en": "I would dare for access hobbies, square brackets, 0.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.22,
          "end": 92.82,
          "en": "With that, if we reload this and take a look at the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.82,
          "end": 94.203,
          "en": "I would see Sports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.21000000000001,
          "end": 100.02000000000001,
          "en": "Now arrays are a super common value type and JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 100.02000000000001,
          "end": 102.99000000000001,
          "en": "because it turns out that you quite often",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.99000000000001,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "need to store a list of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 108.84,
          "en": "For example, in this demo React application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 110.82,
          "en": "I showed you earlier in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.82,
          "end": 113.46000000000001,
          "en": "there also was a content array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.46000000000001,
          "end": 117.81,
          "en": "which actually contained more arrays as values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.81,
          "end": 120.18,
          "en": "because that's all important to know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.18,
          "end": 123.99,
          "en": "arrays can contain any kinds of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.99,
          "end": 128.13,
          "en": "They can contain other arrays, objects, numbers, strings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.13,
          "end": 129.3,
          "en": "whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.3,
          "end": 132.45,
          "en": "Here I have an array of more arrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.45,
          "end": 137.45,
          "en": "and those inner nested arrays then actually contain strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.93,
          "end": 142.38,
          "en": "Now when defining array, the individual values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.38,
          "end": 146.13,
          "en": "that make up the array are separated by commas.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 150.42000000000002,
          "en": "And then as mentioned, you access values by their index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.42000000000002,
          "end": 153.9,
          "en": "Now since arrays are such a super important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.9,
          "end": 156.9,
          "en": "very common value type in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.9,
          "end": 160.86,
          "en": "there actually also are a couple of built-in utility methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.86,
          "end": 164.22,
          "en": "you can use on arrays to transform",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.22,
          "end": 167.61,
          "en": "or read the values stored in the arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.61,
          "end": 170.82,
          "en": "You can access these utility array methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.82,
          "end": 174.54,
          "en": "by using the array name and then the dot notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.54,
          "end": 177.06,
          "en": "And then you should automatically get a suggestion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.06,
          "end": 179.76,
          "en": "of the methods that are available here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.76,
          "end": 182.19,
          "en": "For example, there is the push method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.19,
          "end": 185.13,
          "en": "which allows you to add a new item to an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.13,
          "end": 187.02,
          "en": "For example, Working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 191.04,
          "en": "If I add this here and I then console.log hobbies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.04,
          "end": 192.45,
          "en": "you will see that now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.45,
          "end": 195.84,
          "en": "hobbies here actually contains four elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.84,
          "end": 197.91,
          "en": "therefore ending with the index 3,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.91,
          "end": 200.073,
          "en": "since we start at the index 0.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 204.45,
          "en": "And the last element is this Working string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.45,
          "end": 207.36,
          "en": "I just pushed onto the array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.36,
          "end": 209.46,
          "en": "Now there, of course, are way more methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.46,
          "end": 211.47,
          "en": "and I'm not going to explain them all here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.47,
          "end": 213.87,
          "en": "But, for example, a never method, which you should know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.87,
          "end": 216.03,
          "en": "which can be quite useful sometimes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 216.03,
          "end": 218.88,
          "en": "is the findIndex method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.88,
          "end": 222.36,
          "en": "This is a method that allows you to find the index",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.36,
          "end": 223.563,
          "en": "of a certain value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.57999999999998,
          "end": 228.99,
          "en": "For this, findIndex actually takes a function as an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 228.99,
          "end": 232.35,
          "en": "and that's a great use case for using such a arrow function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.35,
          "end": 234.21,
          "en": "since it's super short to write",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 234.21,
          "end": 236.52,
          "en": "and not a lot of characters to type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.52,
          "end": 239.52,
          "en": "This arrow function, which you pass to findIndex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.52,
          "end": 242.94,
          "en": "should accept at least one input parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 242.94,
          "end": 245.01,
          "en": "which could be called item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.01,
          "end": 247.41,
          "en": "because findIndex behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 247.41,
          "end": 249.45,
          "en": "will execute this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.45,
          "end": 251.76,
          "en": "which you're passing to findIndex,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 251.76,
          "end": 254.25,
          "en": "and will automatically provide a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 254.25,
          "end": 256.23,
          "en": "for this input parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 256.23,
          "end": 259.02,
          "en": "Therefore, of course, your function also must accept it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 259.02,
          "end": 261.9,
          "en": "in order to then use it in this function body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 261.9,
          "end": 265.11,
          "en": "Now, in this function body, in case of findIndex,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 265.11,
          "end": 269.04,
          "en": "you then should return true if you have the item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 269.04,
          "end": 272.94,
          "en": "that you were looking for, and false otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.94,
          "end": 277.94,
          "en": "For that, we can return item === 'Sports', For example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.97,
          "end": 283.23,
          "en": "if we were looking for the index of the item Sports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 283.23,
          "end": 285.75,
          "en": "So if we were looking for the index of this item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285.75,
          "end": 287.76,
          "en": "What this code here does is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 287.76,
          "end": 291.99,
          "en": "it executes this function automatically behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.99,
          "end": 296.07,
          "en": "for every item in this array, including this Working item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 296.07,
          "end": 298.68,
          "en": "which was pushed onto the array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 298.68,
          "end": 301.95,
          "en": "And then for every item, it compares that item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 301.95,
          "end": 304.71,
          "en": "So that text here to this text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 304.71,
          "end": 306.54,
          "en": "with help of this comparison operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 306.54,
          "end": 307.803,
          "en": "which I mentioned before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 309.09,
          "end": 313.5,
          "en": "If the two are equal, this function here returns true,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.5,
          "end": 315.36,
          "en": "and therefore findIndex knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 315.36,
          "end": 317.73,
          "en": "that I found the item I was looking for,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 317.73,
          "end": 321.51,
          "en": "and it will then give me the index of that item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.51,
          "end": 323.49,
          "en": "Otherwise, this will return false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 323.49,
          "end": 326.043,
          "en": "and findIndex will do nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 327.18,
          "end": 330.67,
          "en": "So, therefore, here I could store that index in a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 332.90999999999997,
          "end": 334.443,
          "en": "and then console.log it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 335.79,
          "end": 339.06,
          "en": "If I save that here, I get 0",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 339.06,
          "end": 340.71,
          "en": "because indeed Sports,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.71,
          "end": 344.1,
          "en": "which is the item I'm looking for here, has the index 0",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 344.1,
          "end": 347.07,
          "en": "since it's the first item in that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 347.07,
          "end": 348.84000000000003,
          "en": "Now this code can definitely be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 348.84000000000003,
          "end": 351.21,
          "en": "a bit more challenging to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 351.21,
          "end": 354.18,
          "en": "since we're passing a function to another function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 354.18,
          "end": 356.85,
          "en": "and that's also something i'll get back to a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 356.85,
          "end": 359.01,
          "en": "later in this section again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 359.01,
          "end": 361.17,
          "en": "But in the end, all that's happening here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 361.17,
          "end": 363.78,
          "en": "is that findIndex needs a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 363.78,
          "end": 366.51,
          "en": "which it can execute on our behalf,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 366.51,
          "end": 368.34,
          "en": "and it will execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 368.34,
          "end": 370.95,
          "en": "for every item in this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 370.95,
          "end": 374.46,
          "en": "It will pass that item for every execution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 374.46,
          "end": 376.23,
          "en": "into that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 376.23,
          "end": 378.57,
          "en": "And, therefore, of course, item will be different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 378.57,
          "end": 379.86,
          "en": "for every execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 379.86,
          "end": 382.47,
          "en": "It will be those items here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 382.47,
          "end": 384.84,
          "en": "And then we compare the item we're getting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 384.84,
          "end": 387.75,
          "en": "to some value we are looking for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 387.75,
          "end": 390.21,
          "en": "So this value we're looking for, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 390.21,
          "end": 392.613,
          "en": "is defined by us, the developer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 393.87,
          "end": 396.213,
          "en": "That's how this function here works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 397.14,
          "end": 399.54,
          "en": "Now as a side note, if you have code like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 399.54,
          "end": 403.47,
          "en": "an arrow function where all you do in the function body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 403.47,
          "end": 407.01,
          "en": "so between these curly braces, is return something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 407.01,
          "end": 409.26,
          "en": "you can even shorten this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 409.26,
          "end": 411.21,
          "en": "and get rid of the return statement",
